  "body": "Updated `spectrum` interface and algorithm.\r\n\r\n**NB**: spectrum now requires input files `pmp_info.json` and `c_minus_By.json`, and thus is incompatible with SDPB 3.0 and older versions.\r\n\r\n## Updated command-line options\r\nChanged spectrum command-line options (call `spectrum --help` for details):\r\n- Instead of PMP file `--input path/to/pmp.nsv`, you should provide `--pmpInfo path/to/sdp/pmp_info.json` \r\n- If `--lambda=false`, you may omit `--solution` and specify only `--cMinusBy` (Path to `c_minus_By.json` with the block vector `(c - B.y)`)\r\n- Added option `--maxZero` to ignore zeros that are too large. `--maxZero 0` means no limit.\r\n- `--meshThreshold` is marked is obsolete.\r\n\r\n## New dependencies\r\n- [MPSolve](https://github.com/robol/MPSolve) (3.2.2 or later), see updated installation instructions in [Install.md](https://github.com/davidsd/sdpb/blob/bdceddb05b43438f60304a763f75ca0bbe5175cf/Install.md#L105)\r\n\r\n## Changes in algorithm\r\n- Find minima of a polynomial `det (c-B.y)` using MPSolve. This makes finding zeros faster and more reliable than an old custom mesh algorithm.\r\n- The new algorithm can also find isolated zeros, see #153",
